      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Typescript is an illusion - it only exists at compile time.\n\nIt is closer to a testing tool than it is a programming language.\n\nWe use types to specify the set of allowable values for an operation,\ndata type, etc.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Typescript is an illusion - it only exists at compile time.\n\nIt is closer to a testing tool than it is a programming language.\n\nWe use types to specify the set of allowable values for an operation,\ndata type, etc.",
